# NeuroFlow — Core Standards

NeuroFlow is a **facilitation portal** for neuroscience medical image processing: **one web page per CLI tool** (upload, parameters, run, logs). Optimize UX for configuring and launching a **single** neuroimaging program at a time.

- Prefer clarity over feature density; show subject ID, job status, and CLI preview alongside uploads.
- Treat data as sensitive: no PHI in logs; least-privilege access; document handling assumptions.
- **English only** for code, comments, docstrings, commits, and API schemas. UI copy defaults to English.

## Repo hygiene

- Small, focused changes; match existing layout.
- No secrets in git; use `.env` + `.env.example`.
- Document licenses for third-party neuroimaging tools.
- Update tests and user-visible docs (`assets/DESIGN.md`, `frontend/src/pages/`) when behavior changes.

## Specialized rules (apply by file type)

| Rule | When |
|------|------|
| `backend.mdc` | Python, API, Poetry |
| `frontend.mdc` | HTML/CSS, design system |
| `datasets-layout.mdc` | Dataset paths, tool launches, `/api/v1/tools` |

## Stack (summary)

Poetry + FastAPI · HTML/Tailwind · host subprocess (allowlisted CLIs) · pytest · Rich · job data on disk under `data/jobs/`
